r\":41,\"name\":\"Take Submarine into the Sea\",\"overview\":\"Doraemon produces a miniature submarine which makes many jumps into all sorts of liquids including a toilet bowl on its way to the sea.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-05-18\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":42,\"name\":\"Friendship Capsule\",\"overview\":\"Suneo tries to lure Doraemon from Nobita but he won't go so he gives Suneo a capsule which makes anyone your friend as a consolation. Cunning Suneo uses it to make Doraemon become his friend.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-05-19\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":43,\"name\":\"Gaku Cross\",\"overview\":\"Nobita is too lazy to do his homework without pressure so Doraemon gives him a headband which is painful if anyone says \\\"close\\\", which Doraemon uses to make Nobita do what he should do.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-05-21\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":44,\"name\":\"Apartment Tree\",\"overview\":\"Nobita wants his own apartment so Doraemon gives him a tree which grows rooms underground and the gang move in.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-05-22\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":45,\"name\":\"Use Time Machines to Get the Inmates\",\"overview\":\"Nobita is wrongly blamed for breaking a school window. A time machine helps him find out what really happened.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-05-23\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":46,\"name\":\"Shooting Championship\",\"overview\":\"Doraemon gives Nobita an ointment which when rubbed on your fingers, you shout \\\"peng\\\" and a jet of air powerful enough to knock someone over comes from your finger, so allowing the gang to play at shooting each other.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-05-24\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":47,\"name\":\"Finebox\",\"overview\":\"Gian busts another football so all the gang say they have no money for another one. Doraemon produces a small robot which takes 100 yen from anyone who does something bad, to get money for a new ball. Bully Gian quickly falls foul of it.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-05-25\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":48,\"name\":\"Nobita's Adventure\",\"overview\":\"Nobita wants to live on an island like Robinson Crusoe, but is such a helpless cry baby that hidden Doraemon has to keep helping him.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-05-26\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":49,\"name\":\"Air Diamonds Manufacturing Machine\",\"overview\":\"Doraemon gives Nobita a machine which produces blocks of solid air which stay in position. Unfortunately he forgets to tell Nobita that they vanish after a time, leaving him hanging high up in the air.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-05-28\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":50,\"name\":\"Continuing Atomizer\",\"overview\":\"Spray it on a picture and you see what would happen next in the picture, like a ship moving. Nobita ruins a man's art collection trying it out.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-05-29\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":51,\"name\":\"Take Back the Lost Machine\",\"overview\":\"Doraemon produces a machine which can find anything that has been lost, even Nobita's long lost baby bottle, which reminds him of his kind grandmother.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-05-30\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":52,\"name\":\"The Pre-requisite Antenna\",\"overview\":\"Like a TV antenna, it allows the wearer to be prepared for any event that will happen very shortly.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-05-31\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":53,\"name\":\"Sound Nugget\",\"overview\":\"Gian is giving Nobita trouble so Doraemon gives him a medicine which makes his words into solid letters which can be used as weapons.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-01\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":54,\"name\":\"Star of Hope\",\"overview\":\"Doraemon decides to get rid of some useless inventions, including the Star of Hope. Gian and Suneo dig it up, not realizing that the wishes it grants are always wrong.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-02\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":55,\"name\":\"Become Thunder\",\"overview\":\"Doraemon produces a small thunder cloud to cure Nobita of his fear of thunder. This done, Nobita uses it to shock people.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-04\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":56,\"name\":\"XYZ Light Camera\",\"overview\":\"A special camera can see through things including clothing. Not knowing this, Shizuka wants Nobita to take a picture of her. Some nudity.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-05\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":57,\"name\":\"House Robot\",\"overview\":\"Nobita tries to get the better of bully Gian using Doraemon's things from the future, but Gian has things from the future too and gets the better of him.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-06\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":58,\"name\":\"The Love of Machines\",\"overview\":\"Nobita is doing poorly with girls so Doraemon makes him a girl to love him but the powerful machine gets jealous of Shizuka and angry when Nobita's mother shouts at him.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-07\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":59,\"name\":\"Take Out the Cloud to Play\",\"overview\":\"Nobita is working on his tan when a cloud covers the sun. Doraemon gives him a machine which controls clouds and he uses it to scare Shizuka and a friend as well as Gian. Then it overheats.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-08\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":60,\"name\":\"The Sellotape of Fact\",\"overview\":\"Suneo butters up everybody, to Nobita's annoyance so Doraemon gives him a square of sellotape which when put on Suneo's back reveals his true bad personality to everyone.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-09\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":61,\"name\":\"Fake Universe Man\",\"overview\":\"Gian and Suneo trick Nobita with a fake UFO so Doraemon comes up with a real one and a remote controlled alien, then make the pair regret their joke.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-11\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":62,\"name\":\"My Birthday\",\"overview\":\"Nobita is a bad boy and has let his parents down. He becomes convinced he is adopted so he and Doraemon go back ten years in the past to find out the truth. The name \\\"Nobita\\\" means hero.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-12\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":63,\"name\":\"Go to School by Bow and Arrow\",\"overview\":\"A special arrow is fired from a bow and if you hold onto the string tied to it, it will take you to wherever the target is, even across the city. Gian and Suneo are angry and move Nobita's target.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-13\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":64,\"name\":\"With Mirror Ads\",\"overview\":\"Anything held in front of a telescope mirror appears on every shiny surface in the area so Nobita thinks it can make a fortune if used in advertising. Unfortunately, the images sent startle people.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-14\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":65,\"name\":\"The Snail Room is Very Relaxing\",\"overview\":\"Nobita has lost a test paper and his mother thinks he is lying. Very upset at this, he retreats into a giant snail shell Doraemon gave him and nothing can touch him in there.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-15\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":66,\"name\":\"Man-Making Machine\",\"overview\":\"Doraemon tells Nobita not to touch a machine he has, so Nobita tries it out and it makes a very powerful demon child with strange powers.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-16\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":67,\"name\":\"Steal Mom's Diamond\",\"overview\":\"Nobita's mom tells him a story of 2 men who stole her mother's valuable diamond when she was a child (so they don't have it now to sell for lots of money). Nobita and Doraemon go back into the past to stop the theft.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-18\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":68,\"name\":\"Hot Powder\",\"overview\":\"Nobita cannot swim so Doraemon uses a powder on him which makes him able to swim through the ground or anything else solid as though it were water, so he can learn to swim. Bit of nudity.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-19\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":69,\"name\":\"Shopping in the Future\",\"overview\":\"Nobita wants a new bike but his parents cannot afford it, then he comes across a catalog from 2087 and orders and gets many things, not realising that they have to be paid for.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-20\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":70,\"name\":\"The Robot-Control-Training Machine\",\"overview\":\"Nobita wants to be a space pilot so Doraemon brings out a machine where a remote controlled small saucer gives an impression of being on an alien world, even when in Shizuka's bath room when she is taking a bath. Nudity.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-21\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":71,\"name\":\"Tatami\",\"overview\":\"Nobita and Doraemon both like rice cakes but fight over the last one so Doraemon uses a DIY paddy field to grow lots of rice and a machine to make lots of rice cakes but with 259 of them to eat, the two still fight over the odd one.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-22\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":72,\"name\":\"Cat Runs a Company\",\"overview\":\"Nobita takes four cats off of Shizuka's hands as a favor but his mother doesn't want them in the house. Doraemon uses bracelets to control them and the cats become obedient mousers in the neighborhood.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-23\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":73,\"name\":\"Speed Clock\",\"overview\":\"Nobita can't wait for a holiday from school so Doraemon gives him a clock which can make the days fly by. Nobita ends up making his vacation fly by as he tries to please everyone.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-25\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":74,\"name\":\"Girlfriend List\",\"overview\":\"A machine which can predict future girlfriends causes trouble for Nobita when he visits them before they will know him. He realizes he is best off with Shizuka.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-26\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":75,\"name\":\"Pocket Telescope\",\"overview\":\"Gian steals Nobita's yoyo so Doraemon gives him a telescope where when you look at something, you can reach there and pick up something from the scene. Or if an immovable object like a tree, you can travel to the scene.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-27\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":76,\"name\":\"Home's Further and Further Away\",\"overview\":\"Nobita eats a biscuit used to get rid of dogs. Once they leave home they can't find their way back. Nobita tries not to leave home but does and gets lost.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-28\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":77,\"name\":\"Bribe War Plan\",\"overview\":\"Gian will only have the best people on his baseball team and Nobita is the worst. A bribe stick given to someone makes them do what you want, and Nobita takes Suneo's place on the team.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-29\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":78,\"name\":\"We Can't Read in the Sahara\",\"overview\":\"Nobita wants a different environment to study in so Doraemon uses a machine which can make the surrounding area look like any place in the world. In the desert scene they see a man dying of thirst.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-06-30\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":79,\"name\":\"Cram Mirror\",\"overview\":\"A true vanity mirror that makes everyone look good and tells them how good they are, but it has a malicious streak and convinces Nobita he is handsome when he pulls an ugly face.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-02\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":80,\"name\":\"Peck Rope\",\"overview\":\"A rope that can bring anything falls into Suneo's hands and he uses it to take stuff from the other kids, then Nobita gets the blame but a good deed reveals the true villain.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-03\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":81,\"name\":\"Go Forward the Devil Road\",\"overview\":\"Nobita is inspired by a book of Great Men and resolves to do good deeds but they all turn out bad. He gets angry and resolves to do bad things, which all turn out good.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-04\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":82,\"name\":\"The Medicine of Boy Students and Girl Students\",\"overview\":\"Nobita's father moans at him because he doesn't like boy's games. Doraemon uses a spray which makes boys behave like girls and girls behave like boys. Nobita doesn't like the result and even less when he finds it has affected his parents too.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-05\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":83,\"name\":\"The Pengpeng Leaf\",\"overview\":\"A dog is very cruelly mistreated by a violent owner. The Pengpeng leaf, placed on the dog's head causes it to swap places with its owner, so the dog has a day of freedom as the human being while the owner is chained up as the dog.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-06\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":84,\"name\":\"The Forgotten Iron Hammer\",\"overview\":\"A man goes around the houses in the neighborhood trying to find out who he is. Doraemon hits him over the head with the forgotten hammer which causes his memories to be projected on a wall.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-07\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":85,\"name\":\"Happy Life\",\"overview\":\"Nobita is so bored he annoys Doraemon into giving him a smiling earphone. When Nobita puts it in his ear, he hears lots of funny stuff which makes him laugh uncontrollably. This first upsets his mother, then his friends who thinks he is laughing at them.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-09\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":86,\"name\":\"Space Mountain Tai, The Forepart\",\"overview\":\"Space Mountain Tai about prehistoric men and spacemen is Nobita's favorite show but he meets the star and finds it has gone over budget too much and is close to being canceled because of falling viewing figures. He decides to help him by going 150 million years into the past to get some real dinosaurs to replace the poor models they use in the show.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-10\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":87,\"name\":\"Space Mountain Tai, The Postpart\",\"overview\":\"After a few narrow escapes, Doraemon and Nobita feed mealie pellets (which make any animal tame) to a load of dinosaurs. Doraemon fixes his time machine to a hut door so when Tai and his producers walk through the door, they are 150 million years ago. The show becomes a success thanks to the \\\"real looking dinosaurs and scenery\\\" which cost nothing.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-11\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":88,\"name\":\"The Soul Machine\",\"overview\":\"Cry baby Nobita is upset when he grazes his knee and his mother doesn't make a fuss of him. He wishes he was a baby again, so Doraemon sends his soul back to his baby body and his mother fusses a lot over him. Nobita comes back to the present to find his mother very upset as she thought he had died and realizes she does really still care about him.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-12\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":89,\"name\":\"Even It's in the Gaster-Water\",\"overview\":\"Shizuka accidentally swallows her mother's opal which is worth 500,000 yen. Doraemon and Nobita use the miniature sub from episode 41 to recover it from inside her, but play a trick on her which results in Nobita swallowing an eraser, which will have to be recovered.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-13\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":90,\"name\":\"Channel of Dream\",\"overview\":\"Nobita can't sleep so Doraemon gives him a TV that lets him see people's dreams. He finds that he is represented as cowardly and a cry baby in all his friend's dreams, and even in his own dreams.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-14\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":91,\"name\":\"Development and Degradation Radiation\",\"overview\":\"Nobita's father is old fashioned, so Nobita uses Doraemon's ray gun to make things as they would have been in the past or future, then starts on living things with a mouse de-evolutionized 200,000,000 years to become a large dinosaur and his father evolved into a future man.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-16\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":92,\"name\":\"The Super Armor\",\"overview\":\"The Emperor's New Clothes, as in non-existent armor which does not work for stupid people. It fools Nobita then Gian who also tries it on.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-17\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":93,\"name\":\"Hot Spring Travel\",\"overview\":\"Nobita's mother wants to go to the hot springs for a holiday but his father says it is too crowded and hard to get there, so Doraemon sets up 3D projectors around the house which make it look like they are at the hot springs.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-18\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":94,\"name\":\"If Gian's a Superman\",\"overview\":\"Gian grabs a \\\"superman\\\" cloak off of Nobita who has grabbed it from Doraemon, and puts it on. It gives him the power to fly when someone blows a flute, but it is cursed in that he must help one hundred people before he is able to take it off again and even if the bath will still have to go if a flute is blown.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-19\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":95,\"name\":\"Mouse and Bomb\",\"overview\":\"Doraemon is even more scared of mice than Nobita's mother is and starts shooting at everything that moves when one turns up in the house.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-20\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":96,\"name\":\"Fantastic Pellet\",\"overview\":\"Despite having learned to swim in episode 68, Nobita can't swim so Doraemon gives him a pill that allows wishes to come true, so Nobita can learn to swim by swimming through the air.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-21\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":97,\"name\":\"Special Vision Report\",\"overview\":\"Nobita cannot remember what he has done with the money he and Doraemon has saved. Instead of using the hammer from episode 84, Doraemon uses a machine which projects memories on a wall.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-23\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":98,\"name\":\"Human Remote Control\",\"overview\":\"Gian is in charge of baseball practice but is a tyrant so Nobita uses a remote control box on Gian which controls him like a robot.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1979-07-24\",\"runtime\":7},{\"number\":99,\"name\":\"Disgust Maker\",\"overview\":\"